      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Jack and Keith,\n\nCan you take a look at this and let me know your initial thoughts? After chatting with Jack over VC, we think I need to bring back STATE_S5S3/S3S5 at least for ARM. Making Intel devices always go through S4 I think makes sense, but on ARM devices there really is no S4 state, so churning the world to transition through a fake state there seems unnecessary. There are also some other cases to handle, like whether to treat S4 as a SOFT_OFF case or SUSPEND (I chose soft off here), and whether to run the chipset off hooks when we reach S4 (I think no?).",
